    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d962">

                <pb facs="1116" n="922" xml:id="pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/7–3045</note>
                <head>No. 962<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the United States
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d962-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-30">July 30, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addition to</hi> U. S. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Proposal on German Reparations</hi></p>
                <p>The determination of the amount and character of the industrial capital equipment
                    unnecessary for a peace economy and therefore available for reparation would be
                    made by the Reparation Commission with France added working in consultation with
                    the Control Council subject to the final approval of the zone commander in the
                    zone from which the equipment is to be removed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d962-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d962-f1-content">
                <p>Attachment 4 to the summary of the Tenth Meeting of the Foreign Ministers, July
                    30. See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg488">pp. 488</ref>,
                        <ref target="#pg497">497</ref>. An undated copy in the Pauley Files of the
                    body of this addition bears the following manuscript notation by J. H. Marshall:
                    “Potsdam Draft by Byrnes”. Cf. <ref target="#d961">document No. 961</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
